false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about travel and vacations in social situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn4le09ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Talking About Events in the Past", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Events that happen in your life are called life events. Life events are usually important to remember.<br> You use expressions like <span class=\"italic\"> life-changing</span> or <span class=\"italic\">Did you know that \u2026 ?</span>  to describe key life events.<br><br>You use the Simple Past tense to talk about a finished event or a specific time in the past.<br><br>You can form the regular form of the Simple Past tense by adding <span class=\"strong\">-ed</span> or <span class=\"strong\">-ied</span> to the verb.<br><br>Some verbs are irregular. Their Simple Past form doesn't end in <span class=\"strong\"> -ed</span> or<span class=\"strong\"> -ied</span>, like <span class=\"italic\">came</span> or <span class=\"italic\">was</span> or <span class=\"italic\">won</span>.<br><br>You use wh-questions to ask about past events.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Ann</span>: When was the first time you went on a boat race?<br> <span class=\"strong\">Bob</span>: I participated in the Belize River Challenge. It was a life-changing experience.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Talking About Events in the Present", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Present Simple tense to talk about a routine or a specific action that happens regularly.<br><br>You can use expressions of frequency like <span class=\"italic\">every day</span> or <span class=\"italic\">always</span> with the Present Simple.<br><br>You use the Present Continuous tense to talk about an action happening right now. You can also use the Present Continuous to talk about events that <span class=\"strong\">are happening</span> soon.  You make the Present Continuous with the verb <span class=\"strong\">to be + -ing</span>.<br><br>You use wh-questions to ask about life events in the present.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Simple\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The race commemorates the Maya tradition. <br><br> Sally travels every month for work.<br><br>  Peter spends a lot of time in the office.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">People are commemorating the Maya heritage  today. <br><br> Sally is traveling through Europe right now. <br><br> Vanessa is spending the summer in San Francisco.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Bob</span>: Where are you traveling to next?<br> <span class=\"strong\">Ann</span>: I'm leaving for Mexico tomorrow.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "handmade ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "made by hand not machine ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You can buy handmade goods at the market.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le09ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words to review!", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "tourist season", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a popular time of the year for tourists ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: July is our tourist season.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le09ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to grow tired of ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to become bored with something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I grew tired of London and its gray skies", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le09ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "remarkable", "type": "name"}, {"content": "important; easy to remember", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Mayan culture is remarkable.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le09ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "legacy ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something received from past generations", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The River Challenge celebrates the Mayan legacy in Belize.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le09ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to commemorate ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to celebrate; to honor ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The race commemorates the Maya tradition.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le09ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "civilization", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the culture and history of a group of people ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Mayan civilization was fascinating.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le09ob11aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "life-changing", "type": "name"}, {"content": "very important; an event that changes your life ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The River Challenge was a life-changing experience.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le09ob11aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "memorable ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something you remember for a long time ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The trip was memorable!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le09ob11aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "I'm having the time of my life! ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "I'm having a lot of fun! ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Belize River Challenge is exciting. I'm having the time of my life!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le09ob11aud10", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write an interview with your partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Think of a life-changing event or make one up.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask 4-5 questions about the event. Use <span class=\"italic\">wh-</span> questions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read the dialogue aloud with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Switch roles with your partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I do an interview.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask personal questions about a past life event.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I answer questions as the interviewee.", "type": "text"}]}]}